# 1. In:
# The user enters a multi-digit number when prompted at runtime.

# 2. Process:
# The input is taken as a string, converted to a sorted list of characters/digits, 
# and joined back into a string to preserve digit order.

# 3. Out:
# A welcome message guiding the user, followed by the sorted sequence of digits displayed on screen.

# 4. My message, and why:
# "Welcome to the Digit Sorting Utility!"
# I chose this welcome message because it clearly tells the user what the program does right when it starts.


# Your code below

# Welcome message
print("Welcome to the Digit Sorting Utility!")

# 1. Input: Ask the user for a multi-digit number
number_input = input("Please enter a multi-digit number (e.g., 58214): ")

# 2. Process: Sort the digits in ascending order
# sorted() converts the text into a sorted list of character digits
sorted_digits = sorted(number_input)
# .join() recombines the list back into a single string
ordered_number = "".join(sorted_digits)

# 3. Output: Display the result with a message
print("Success! Your digits have been sorted in ascending order:", {ordered_number})